    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0434" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg326"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August 22, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction, numbered 93,
                    of 1st instant, I have the honor to inclose herewith copies of notes exchanged
                    between <pb facs="0435" n="327" xml:id="pg327"/> the foreign office and myself,
                    relative to the protection of citizens of the United States in Bulgaria.</p>
                <p>You will observe that instructions will at once be sent to Mr. Dering, Her
                    Majesty’s agent and consul-general at Sofia, to continue to our citizens in
                    Bulgaria the same protection that was afforded by his predecessor, Mr.
                    O’Conor.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d321-a1.xml" xpointer="d321-a1"/>
